    "https://jobs.wisc.edu/workwithbucky": {
      "title": "Why ShouldYouWork With Bucky?",
      "description": "Work With Bucky Skip to main content Browse All Jobs Job Alerts Login Kiosk mode Why Should You Work With Bucky? UW–Madison offers a wide range of professions that cover various interests and skill levels. We employ everything from accountants to arborists, chefs to custodians, editors to electricians, graphic designers to groundskeepers, HR associates to HVAC technicians, librarians to locksmiths, mechanics to medical assistants, painters to police officers, web designers to welders, and absolutely everything in between! No matter what you are looking for professionally, chances are you will not only find it but will thrive at it while working at the University of Wisconsin–Madison. Don’t just take our word for it. Here is what a few of our employees have to say about working with Bucky. Ready to view open jobs and apply? Click the “Browse All jobs” button now! Browse All Jobs Have questions about jobs at UW-Madison? Click the button below to complete a brief survey, and a member of the Work With Bucky team will reach out to discuss your job search! We can answer those questions, help you create a job alert, understand the application process, and explain what to expect during the recruitment process. Request an Appointment Prefer to connect in-person? Once a month on Wednesdays from 3:30-4:30 pm, the Work With Bucky team visits the UW South Madison Partnership. No appointment is needed to stop in to chat. Here are our upcoming 2026 dates: September 23 October 14 November 18 December 16 The address is 2238 S Park St, Madison, WI. We can be found on the lower level of the building, room 103. Enter through the Atrium doors and go directly downstairs. Free parking is available! One of the most rewarding aspects for me working at UW–Madison has been this ability to collaborate with colleagues who are as excited and passionate and enthusiastic about taking care of students. The energy from students is contagious. They're at a point in their lives where they're really wanting to see things being done differently. I think that helps us all stay innovative and looking at different initiatives that we can work on together. Ritu B. Associate Director of Psychiatric Services, Clinical Associate Professor One of the things that I'm most proud of in my role as executive chef is the teams that I work with, the teams that I collaborate with. The people that I work with make it easy to come to work every day. Kris E. Executive Chef What keeps me motivated about working at UW–Madison is the impact that I can make. I think I'm a very mission and value driven person, and knowing that my work is contributing towards the greater good of the Madison community and beyond is something that keeps me coming back and keeps me engaged in my work. Sebastian K.-M. Outreach & Sourcing Specialist It's really fascinating just to hear what a reach our university has. Not only within our local community, but across the world as a whole and just the respect and the reputation that this university has. Sarah B. Employee Accommodation Specialist University is a great place to work. A great environment. Beautiful places. Beautiful buildings. A lot of history. Something different every day. You get to meet someone different every day. You learn something different every day. Juan A. Lieutenant, Special Events I'm extremely proud to work for UW–Madison. Off hours when you're maybe coming to a sporting event here on campus and you're with friends and family, getting to be like, hey, that's where I work. It's a beautiful campus and I'm very proud to be part of it. Jason R. Trades Supervisor Be a part of a winning team! Working at UW is fantastic and so are the benefits we offer. As one of the largest employers in Wisconsin, UW–Madison takes pride in fostering a stable work environment, ensuring employees can focus on what they do best. Our employees enjoy competitive salaries, state group healthcare plans, professional development opportunities, and much more. UW–Madison is dedicated to excellence, innovation, and the Wisconsin Idea. Take the next step of your professional journey where skills meet endless possibilities, and aspirations become reality. Join a winning team that values your potential and invests in your future. Your next career is just a few clicks away. Apply today and Work with Bucky! Browse All Jobs Disability Accommodations To request a disability or pregnancy-related accommodation for any step in the hiring process (e.g., application, interview, pre-employment testing, etc.), please contact the Divisional Disability Representative (DDR) in the division you are applying to. Please make your request as soon as possible to help the university respond most effectively to you. Language Services English If you have questions please contact the Office of Human Resources at 608-265-2257 or uwjobs@wisc.edu . Please call Cultural Linguistic Services if you need assistance in Spanish (Español 608-263-2328, 608-263-0623 o 608-265-0838), Hmong (Hmoob 608-263-2217), Tibetan (བོད་ཡིག 608-890-2545), Chinese (汉语 608-890-2628), or Nepali (नेपाली 608-262-7521). Español / Spanish Si tiene preguntas por favor póngase en contacto con la Oficina de Recursos Humanos llamando al 608-265-2257 o mande un correo electrónico a: spanish-cls@wisc.edu . Si necesita ayuda en español llame a Servicios Lingüísticos y Culturales al teléfono 608-265-1489 o al 608-265-0838. Hmoob / Hmong Yog koj muaj lus nug thov hu rau Office of Human Resources 608-265-2257 los hmong-cls@wisc.edu . Yog koj xav tau kev pab rau lus Hmoob, thov hu rau Cultural Linguistic Services 608-263-2217. བོད་ཡིག / Tibetan དྲི་བ་ཡོད ་ཚེ། ལས་བྱེད་བདག་གཉེར་ཡིག་ཚང་ལ་ཁ་པར་ ༦༠༨ ༢༦༥ ༢༢༥༧ དང་ཡང་ན་གློག་འཕྲིན་ tibetan-cls@wisc.edu ཐོག་འབྲེལ་བ་གནང་རོགས། གལ་སྲིད་ཁྱེད་ལ་བོད་སྐད་ཀྱི་སྐད་སྒྱུར་རོགས་རམ་དགོས་ཚེ། རིག་གཞུང་སྐད་ཡིག་ཞབས་ཞུ་ཁང་གི་ཁ་པར་ ༦༠༨ ༨༩༠ ༢༥༤༥ ལ་འབྲེལ་བ་ གནང་རོགས་ཞུ།། 中文 / Chinese 如果您有问题，请联系人力资源办公室（608-265-2257 或 chinese-cls@wisc.edu ）。如果您需要汉语服务，请联系文化语言服务中心，电话 608-890-2628。 नेपाली / Nepali यदि तपाईंसँग प्रश्नहरू छन् भने कृपया मानव संसाधनको कार्यालयलाई 608-265-2257 मा फोन वा nepali-cls@wisc.edu मा ईमेल मार्फत सम्पर्क गर्नुहोला । यदि तपाईंलाई नेपाली भाषामा सहयोगको आवश्यकता छ भने कृपया सांस्कृतिक भाषागत सेवा (Cultural Linguistic Services) 608-262-7521 मा फोन गर्नुहोला । Footer Crest Quick Links Madison, WI About UW Visit Campus Employee Benefits Working at UW Contact Talent Acquisition Office of Human Resources University of Wisconsin–Madison 21 N. Park Street, Suite 5101 Madison, WI 53715-1218 Website feedback, questions or accessibility issues: ohrwebmaster@ohr.wisc.edu . Learn more about accessibility at UW–Madison . © 2016–2026 Board of Regents of the University of Wisconsin System • Privacy Statement Candidate Details We use cookies on this site. By continuing to browse without changing your browser settings to block or delete cookies, you agree to the UW–Madison Privacy Notice . I do not accept I accept"
    },
